        "Dawn on Plate Four is a rumor the rain grid has not approved yet. The light that arrives is the color of watered milk. Mia is already awake, because nurses are. She is at the kettle again. The paper towel from the clinic is not here; the words SAFE and RUN are in her head now, or the envelope is behind her manuals, or both.\n\n\"Eat,\" she says, and puts toast on a plate that has a hairline crack. You eat. It tastes like a life you could have kept if you were a different animal. The toast's crack is louder than it should be. You butter it with a knife that has cut fruit and nothing else, and you are grateful for the limitation. Outside, a tram that does not care about galas leans through a curve. She eats standing, a nurse's breakfast, already halfway to the next wrist. Crumbs on the cracked plate look like a map of a smaller country. You do not sweep them. Sweeping would be staying.",
        "She studies {{him}} in the milk-light the way she studied the bruise. \"Whatever they do to you at that gala, your face will try to come back here. Faces do that. Don't let a firm tell you that's weakness. It's navigation.\" She packs her bag for the next shift: badge, lotion, the pencil for her hair, a knife that is technically for fruit. \"I am going to work. You are going to a glass room. If you die, I will be inconvenient. If you live, you will text me a word that isn't a joke.\"\n\nYou almost say her name like an apology. She shakes her head. \"Don't. Apologies are for people who plan to stop. Just go become whatever they paid for, and then come back ugly. I can work with ugly. I cannot work with missing.\" She slings the bag. The fruit knife clicks against the badge. You almost ask to see her to the clinic and stop, because that would be a second photograph. She sees the almost and nods, which is permission to be a coward in the correct direction.",
